From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH kbase-common 005] panvk: enumerate /dev/mali* kbase nodes

Purpose: Enumerate Kbase non-DRM nodes (/dev/mali0..7) alongside DRM
 render nodes during vkEnumeratePhysicalDevices, via the common
 .enumerate hook. Adds PANVK_DEBUG_KBASE_DIAG as a NEW bit 20 (does not
 rename upstream flags, unlike the reference).
Source/Reference: https://github.com/wonderkast02/panvk-g720-kbase-csf
 branch android-candidate-beta-1.9.4
 (src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_instance.[hc]), adapted: upstream copyright,
 pan_trace include/init, dri options and debug-flag names kept; only the
 kbase includes, new debug bit, enumerate function and hook switch taken.
Tested GPU: none yet (compile-level).
Tested Kbase UAPI: n/a.
Mesa base range: 26.3.0-devel (pinned 5a07217f).
Dependencies: 004 (panvk_physical_device_init_kbase).
Validation test: vkEnumeratePhysicalDevices lists Mali on /dev/mali0,
 DRM path unchanged.

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_instance.h b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_instance.h
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_instance.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_instance.h
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
    PANVK_DEBUG_NO_EXTENDED_VA_RANGE = 1 << 17,
    PANVK_DEBUG_HSR_PREPASS = 1 << 18,
    PANVK_DEBUG_NO_CRC = 1 << 19,
+   PANVK_DEBUG_KBASE_DIAG = 1 << 20,
 };

 extern uint64_t panvk_debug;
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_instance.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_instance.c
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_instance.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_instance.c
@@ -15,6 +15,12 @@
 #include "util/os_misc.h"
 #include "util/u_call_once.h"

